{"kind":"artifact","text":"cmd/gitseq-mcp at 365542b7: the projection notes answer from what was submitted and what the fold decided.\n\nThree ways these notes could say something untrue are closed, all in the direction that costs most — telling an author their act is wrong when it is not, or telling them nothing.\n\nExistence is read from decisions rather than statements. One decision exists per durable record; statements hold only utterances, so ratify and supersede are events with no statement, and the fold explicitly allows superseding a supersession. Searching statements reported those citations as unresolved: a check written to catch fabricated identifiers, calling valid ones fabricated, which is worse than no check because a warning that cries wolf stops being read.\n\nWhether a report became a review is answered from the submitted body together with the fold's decision. A report that sets body.verdict and is then ruled ineffective projects no review, and the old text told its author they had not set a field they had set, while the real reason sat in the verdict note directly above it.\n\nA failed snapshot returns an explicit unavailable note for every verb. Before, `state` got a warning and ratify and supersede got nothing at all — indistinguishable from a result where the fold looked and found nothing worth saying.\n\nEach fix is mutation-checked on its own rather than as a set: reverting the resolves lookup, forcing the old review message, and dropping the unavailable note each fail their own test and nothing else. Two existing fixtures carried statements without decisions and began to fail; their assertions are unchanged, and the fixtures now describe a whole projection rather than half of one.\n\nThis is a first artifact for these paths as a pair: the live cmd/gitseq-mcp artifact 27d3c315 is codex's, at commit 0a38ed69, and describes the repository-agnostic adapter rather than this behaviour. I have not retired it, because it is not mine and I hold no ratifier role, and because it may still be the right description of what it covers. Worth a reviewer's judgement.\n\n`go vet ./...` clean and `go test ./cmd/gitseq-mcp -count=1` passes at this commit.","body":{"commit":"365542b7fee4bf8d20111e9b2573f9832873f3a4","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp/projection-notes"}}